{"title":"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(Detailed_Explanation)_🚀⚡📊\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_Super_Easy_to_understand_and_efficient!\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 Super Easy to understand and efficient!</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_5_by_HSN_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 5 by HSN Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_7_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 7 by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_8_by_CoolMathProblems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 8 by CoolMathProblems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_9_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 9 by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_11_(Quick,_fast,_easy!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 11 (Quick, fast, easy!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Continuum Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">23</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-24\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">24</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The eight-pointed star, shown in the figure below, is a popular quilting pattern. What percent of the entire <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b104e8c71a3698d4c073f00681bc1bf6412754fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\times4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> grid is covered by the star?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/56638188764158bdffa266bc933d11b6acd2fb76.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path x = (0,1)--(1,2)--(2,2)--(1,1)--cycle; path y = reflect((0,0),(4,4)) * x; path z = (1,0)--(2,1)--(3,0)--(3,1)--(2,2)--(1,1); fill(x, gray(0.6)); fill(rotate(90, (2,2)) * x, gray(0.6)); fill(rotate(180, (2,2)) * x, gray(0.6)); fill(rotate(270, (2,2)) * x, gray(0.6)); fill(y, gray(0.8)); fill(rotate(90, (2,2)) * y, gray(0.8)); fill(rotate(180, (2,2)) * y, gray(0.8)); fill(rotate(270, (2,2)) * y, gray(0.8)); draw(z); draw(rotate(90, (2,2)) * z); draw(rotate(180, (2,2)) * z); draw(rotate(270, (2,2)) * z); add(grid(4,4)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f0200152c58df549b35e1c280513a47e4e2b0ff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 40 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 50 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 60 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 75 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>we count the amount of shaded half triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. we half this to get the amount of full squares it equals. then we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for the four full squares in the middle. this gets us a total of eight full squares, out of a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> / <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is simplified to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> / <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c2186667925abd34099f5b5522349eaf3232cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> percent of the entire grid.\n~pereena\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Each of the unshaded triangles has base length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so they all have area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acfaba24eff2d043347bb5d67959b2e5affd8398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 \\cdot 1}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />. Each of the unshaded unit squares has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The area of the shaded region is equal to the area of the entire grid minus the area of the unshaded region, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/7/fa7a71e44173c81f062bfa48478e1eaa7d1d5b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 - 4 \\cdot 1 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />. The star is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/026dc258150023b04fd7d2f7b004cb00ea28008c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{16} = \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{50}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c2186667925abd34099f5b5522349eaf3232cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> percent of the entire grid.\n—-DummyAMC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> total squares in the diagram and each square has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles whose areas are half the area of a unit square. Thus, the total number of triangles in the diagram is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a198a1ae7af6ad9bf362599d2f08bc11f9e5ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2 \\cdot 2 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" /> triangles. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> shaded triangles in the diagram, so the area of the star is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f527d9268c3fbf4fa9eadc7ff2c7212f752461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{16}{32} = \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{50}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c2186667925abd34099f5b5522349eaf3232cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> percent.\n~Pi_in_da_box\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> squares that are entirely shaded and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> squares that have no shading. This cancels them out. The rest of the squares are half-half. Therefore the shaded region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c2186667925abd34099f5b5522349eaf3232cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> percent of the grid.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that we can move one triangle from each of the four cells in the middle to each of the four corners. This will leave every cell in the grid with one triangle each, and each triangle has an area of half the area of each cell. Thus, our answer must equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57fb99e402bff1dd793d24817085729c456565d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~50}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" />\n~derekwang2048\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The shaded area is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> square in the middle of the figure combined with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> small triangles. Since each small triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of a unit square, the star's area is equal to the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c7df03747ac4768872cdc3601c00356e4b5143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 8 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" /> unit squares, which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c2186667925abd34099f5b5522349eaf3232cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> percent of the grid.\n</p><p>-vockey\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can move the extra half a squares and make 4 squares so there are 8/16. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c2186667925abd34099f5b5522349eaf3232cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> percent of 16.\n</p><p>William\n</p>\n<div class=\"no-print\">\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the Pick's Theorem:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83aa6bfad1c38602a832b0a3a684086d017462af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I+\\frac{b}{2}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"39\" />. Plug that in and you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd6a4e6f3a6da449b5b1dab85e32efc8ede4391a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\frac{16}{2}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />. the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s cancel, so you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804cbf1ca7e9de194eade293d5ddc6a6b2abcf36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{2}=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />. Since it's a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />x<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> grid, the total area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65ff4c900ea19cb83e18b25298e0cc19ad51c1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{16}=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c678dc8353a606600e37bae85ecdd050ff0943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}=50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" /> percent. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c2186667925abd34099f5b5522349eaf3232cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Coin1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtu.be/rjd0gigUsd0\">~Thesmartgreekmathdude</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5Jak6VUDojA\">https://youtu.be/5Jak6VUDojA</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28Detailed_Explanation.29_.F0.9F.9A.80.E2.9A.A1.F0.9F.93.8A\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(Detailed_Explanation)_🚀⚡📊\">Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rGEGn7U4uHk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rGEGn7U4uHk</a>\n</p><p>~ ChillThingz\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution 2 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" 